  "id": "DrugBank_DB00420 - MONDO_2258",
  "verbalization": "Promazine, a sedative and antipsychotic drug, is associated with the indication of Common Cold through multiple pathways. These pathways link Promazine to Ammonium Chloride, Guaiacol, and Bromodiphenhydramine, all of which are indicated for Pharyngitis. The shared indication of Common Cold across these relationships suggests a potential mechanistic link between Promazine and pharyngeal inflammation. The evidence is supported by the presence of overlapping indications, which may imply that Promazine could influence inflammatory processes in the pharynx through the pathways of these related compounds. The final scores, while not definitive, suggest a plausible association, though further mechanistic validation is required to establish a direct causal relationship. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Promazine to modulate inflammatory responses, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
